  "id": "color-purity",
  "term": "color purity",
  "definition": "Color purity is another name for saturation: how intense or vivid a color appears relative to other colors or dullness. In the source material, it is treated as a way of quantifying color, though its measurement can become difficult when the hue shifts with changing temperature.",
